## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-hop, CKNE-aware backpressure and fairness across thousands of tenants with SLA-based tuning.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health as a control signal for fan-out
- Per-tenant token bucket and dynamic scaling
- SLA-tier influences on limits and queuing
- Edge backpressure signaling and aggregation
- Payload schemas and end-to-end test plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeLimit(health, queueLen, sla) {
  const base = 1000;
  if (health > 0.8 && queueLen < sla.maxQueue * 0.7) return Math.min(base * 5, sla.maxCap);
  if (health < 0.4 || queueLen > sla.maxQueue * 0.9) return Math.max(base * 0.2, sla.minCap);
  return base;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to translate CKNE into concrete tracing budgets and fairness guarantees in a real backend.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE mapping to sampling, retention, storage tier
- Minute-level reallocation with safety guards
- Observability of SLA, budgets, and rollbacks

## Code Example
```javascript
function budgets(ckne, base, max){
  const rate = base + ckne*(max-base);
  const reten = base + ckne*(max-base);
  const hot = base + ckne*(1-base);
  return {rate, reten, hot};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for edge CKNE values and abrupt CKNE shifts?
- What failure modes require automated rollback and how would you detect them?

